  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">An AI suggestion feature with no eval set has no way to know if a prompt or model change made it better or worse until users start complaining — usually weeks after it shipped.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Build a small golden set of real inputs with known-good expected outputs, score every prompt/model change against it automatically, and treat a regression there as a merge blocker, not a lagging indicator.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Grow the golden set from real production failures rather than imagined edge cases, watch for eval sets too small or too easy to catch a real regression, and version/spot-check an LLM judge's own scoring the same way you'd validate any other grader.</div>
